            <ArticleTitle>Surgical repair of coronary artery to pulmonary artery fistula with aneurysms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1089-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejcts.2009.02.033</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 58-year-old female was referred to our hospital with an abnormal shadow on her chest X-ray. Further examination revealed the left anterior descending coronary artery to pulmonary artery fistula with aneurysms. The patient was successfully repaired with operation and had no residual fistulas and aneurysms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
